cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ExactFrac, please cite the software using the metadata in this file."
title: "ExactFrac"
type: software
version: "0.1.0.dev0"

authors:
  - family-names: "Fons"
    given-names: "Cherine"

abstract: >-
  ExactFrac is a research-software development project for an exact,
  certificate-producing implementation of the compact positive-integer-multiplicity
  modified set-pair density problem under the active hypothesis f(v) <= d_q(v).
  The project combines an exact solver architecture with an independent verifier,
  hand-derived oracle cases, adversarial testing, and independently checkable
  witnesses.

repository-code: "https://github.com/Cherine-Fons/ExactFrac"

license: MIT

keywords:
  - combinatorial optimization
  - exact algorithms
  - strongly polynomial algorithms
  - graph algorithms
  - certificate verification
  - compact multiplicities
